# VRM/GLB fixtures are binary — never apply text/EOL conversion.
*.vrm binary
*.glb binary

# USDA fixtures, goldens, and baseline snapshots must check out with LF
# everywhere: a CRLF smudge changes the *content* of multi-line (triple-quoted)
# strings — the \r becomes part of the parsed string value — so a Windows
# checkout would flatten to different bytes than the committed golden
# (vrmschema-pr-windows L5 failure, PR #42).
*.usda text eol=lf

# Capture traces must check out with LF everywhere. The corpus test re-emits
# each committed trace through motionRuntime's writer -- which always writes
# '\n', so a shared fixture is byte-identical across the three OS cells -- and
# compares the raw bytes. A CRLF smudge on a Windows checkout would fail that
# comparison for every trace while the data itself was fine. Same reason as
# *.usda above.
*.trace text eol=lf
